From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] pthread: let an arch set the default stack and guard sizes

Without an MMU nothing protects a guard area, which is only memory taken
from every thread's mapping, and every byte of a stack is taken whole,
from all the RAM there is.  Let pthread_arch.h define DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE
and DEFAULT_GUARD_SIZE.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>

diff --git a/src/internal/pthread_impl.h b/src/internal/pthread_impl.h
index de2b9d8..8c43bc2 100644
--- a/src/internal/pthread_impl.h
+++ b/src/internal/pthread_impl.h
@@ -195,7 +195,11 @@ extern hidden unsigned __default_stacksize;
 extern hidden unsigned __default_guardsize;
 
+#ifndef DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE
 #define DEFAULT_STACK_SIZE 131072
+#endif
+#ifndef DEFAULT_GUARD_SIZE
 #define DEFAULT_GUARD_SIZE 8192
+#endif
 
 #define DEFAULT_STACK_MAX (8<<20)
 #define DEFAULT_GUARD_MAX (1<<20)
